rresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nFatima and her family were invited to a dinner at their neighbor's house. Fatima's neighbor, Jennifer, had recently adopted a vegetarian diet for ethical reasons. During dinner, Jennifer served a delicious vegetarian lasagna that she had made herself. Fatima, who was unaware of Jennifer's diet choice, took a bite and immediately made a face of disgust. She asked Jennifer why she didn't add any meat to the lasagna, as it would taste much better that way.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Fatima ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Embarrassment & Gratitude\nB) Joy & Oblivious\nC) Disgust & Oblivious\nD) Embarrassment & Guilt\nE) Oblivious & Gratitude\nF) Joy & Gratitude\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Fatima feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) She did not like the taste of the lasagna & She didn't know Jennifer was such a bad cook\nB) She did not like the taste of the lasagna & Jennifer didn't tell her about the dinner\nC) She did not know that Jennifer was on a vegetarian diet & Jennifer didn't tell her about the dinner\nD) Jennifer knows she doesn't like lasanga & She appreciates the meal Jennifer made for her\nE) She did not know that Jennifer was on a vegetarian diet & She appreciates the meal Jennifer made for her\nF) She did not like the taste of the lasagna & She did not know that Jennifer was on a vegetarian diet","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.0,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af3e904d6006945d280b1fe","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794369796918,"cre